<h1>Seated Single-Arm Overhead Dumbbell Tricep Extension    </h1>
  <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u> 
This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates the Seated Single-Arm Overhead Dumbbell Tricep Extension. The video highlights the triceps muscle (Triceps Brachii) in bright glowing colors, illustrating how extending the dumbbell vertically overhead puts the long head of the triceps under a deep stretch and maximum mechanical tension.


Target Muscles: Triceps Brachii (especially the Long Head)
Secondary Muscles: Core / Abs (for spinal stabilization), Deltoids (Shoulders)

</div></div>



<h1> How to Perform (Step-by-Step)   </h1>

<u><b><h4>Step 1: Setup</h4></b></u>
Sit upright on a flat bench with your feet planted firmly on the floor. Hold a dumbbell in one hand and raise your arm overhead so it is fully extended toward the ceiling.

<u><b><h4>Step 2: Alignment & Stabilization</h4></b></u> 
Keep your core tight, back straight, and your upper arm close to your head. You can place your non-working hand across your stomach or chest for balance and posture support.

<u><b><h4>Step 3: Lowering Phase (Eccentric)</h4></b></u>
Inhale as you slowly bend your elbow, lowering the dumbbell behind your head in a controlled arc until you feel a deep stretch in your triceps. Keep your upper arm still and pointing upward.

<u><b><h4>Step 4: Extension Phase (Concentric)</h4></b></u>
Exhale as you press the dumbbell back up overhead by driving through your triceps until your arm reaches full extension at the top.



<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

<b>◉Maximum Long Head Stretch:</b> Overhead positioning fully stretches the long head of the triceps, which leads to greater overall arm muscle hypertrophy.<br>

<b>◉Unilateral Muscle Balance:</b> Isolating one arm at a time allows you to identify and fix strength or symmetry gaps between your left and right arms.<br>

<b>◉Seated Back Support:</b> Sitting upright isolates the arm extension movement and reduces momentum or swinging compared to standing overhead extensions.


<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 4 | 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 8 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Keep your upper arm locked in a vertical position next to your head throughout the exercise—only your forearm should move.



